 for Livingston County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September came in at 39% of normal on the middle of the grids, and June to July hit 148%. Grid 23547 had its driest year in 1956 at 55% of normal.</p>"}
